{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>For the Amalekite, etc. For therefore you turned back, etc.</b> The meaning is: since the rebellion was over what the spies said — ״עֲמָלֵק יוֹשֵׁב בְּאֶרֶץ הַנֶּגֶב״ etc. ״and the Canaanite״ etc. — and they said ״וְלָמָּה ה׳ מֵבִיא אוֹתָנוּ לִנְפֹּל בַּחֶרֶב״, if so, how can you trust that HaShem will perform a miracle for you in the very place of the wicked itself? Therefore He said <b>וּנְפַלְתֶּם בַּחֶרֶב</b> — for certain. ״כִּי עַל כֵּן״ — meaning, on account of Amalek dwelling, etc., and the fear of falling by the sword — this was the cause for which you turned back from following HaShem, and assuredly HaShem will not be with you."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:39.163908682Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}